I added `EmptyListMessage` and its light/dark preview in `app/shared/src/commonMain/kotlin/org/jetbrains/kotlinconf/screens/EmptyListMessage.kt`. I could not compile it: the sandbox has no Java runtime, so the Gradle build failed before reaching Kotlin.

```kotlin
@Composable
fun EmptyListMessage(text: String) {
    Box(
        modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize(),
        contentAlignment = Alignment.Center,
    ) {
        Text(
            text = text,
            style = KotlinConfTheme.typography.text1.copy(textAlign = TextAlign.Center),
        )
    }
}

@PreviewLightDark
@Composable
private fun EmptyListMessagePreview() = PreviewHelper {
    EmptyListMessage("No sessions match your filters")
}
```

Choices I made:
- **Centring:** the message fills its parent and centres both ways, with the text itself centre-aligned. That suits an empty-list state that takes the screen's space. If you want it to size to its content, drop the `fillMaxSize()`.
- **Preview:** I reused the existing `PreviewHelper` from `ui-components`. It already applies the app theme, the main background, 8 dp padding and 8 dp spacing, so the preview matches your spec without new layout code. `@PreviewLightDark` gives the light and dark variants.
- **Text:** I used the `ui-components` `Text` with `typography.text1`, the same default the rest of the app uses.

To check it, run `./gradlew :app:shared:compileKotlinJvm` on a machine with a JDK, then open the preview in Android Studio.

