Choices I made:
- **Preview:** I used the existing `PreviewHelper`, which already applies the app theme, the main background, 8 dp padding and 8 dp spacing. `@PreviewLightDark` produces the light and dark variants.
- **Text:** I used the project's own `Text` composable, not Material 3's, because the screens use it. It has no `textAlign` parameter, so the centring comes from the style. Keeping the text in the `text2` style with `secondaryText` colour is also my choice; say if you want a different style or colour.
- **Layout:** The composable fills its parent and centres the text in it, so it works as an empty state in any screen.
- **Preview size:** The preview passes `Modifier.fillMaxSize()` so the message sits centred in the preview window.

